   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## IP-Adapter, and IP-Adapter with the colour held\n\nBoth take something from the same reference picture, but not the same thing. IP-Adapter encodes it with CLIP Vision and feeds the result into the model's attention, which carries **subject, style and texture**. It is famously loose about the palette: the look arrives, the exact colours wander.\n\nThe ColorKit node measures the reference's **colour** and holds the prediction to it. Different hook, different quantity, no conflict — one patches attention, the other patches the noise prediction.\n\nBoth branches run the **same seed**, so the only difference is the colour node. The comparison at the end is the point of the graph.\n\n**Before running:** pick an SDXL checkpoint, and make sure the IP-Adapter models and CLIP Vision are in place — the unified loader will say so if they are not."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
